the rixtag chamber in stockholm was  packed full for the momentous vote  an electronic ballot which took less  than 20 seconds to confirm the outcome  stefan lofvin is the first swedish  premier ever to lose a confidence vote  lofen sat impassively on the front row  as his coalition disintegrated before  his eyes  lofton is a former union boss famed for  his negotiating skills  and since an inconclusive election in  2018 lofthand's social democrats have  governed in a minority coalition with  the greens  while still needing the support of  smaller parties to get votes through  parliament  but his government proposals to reform  sweden's strict  rent control system proved to be a red  line for the left party  who warned that they would bring down  the government unless the proposals were  withdrawn  we kept our word said the left party  leader sir laflin now has one week to  decide whether to call a snap election  or resign and give the speaker of  parliament the task of trying to find a  replacement prime minister  was it bored regardless of what happens  now my party and myself  will together with others be available  to shoulder the responsibility of  leading the country  my primary focus has always been is and  will always be to do what is best for  sweden  that's a heavy hint of what many  analysts are suggesting  that with sweden's fragmented political  landscape and opinion polls showing the  centre-left and centre-right blocks  evenly balanced  it's entirely possible that the speaker  will hand the top job back  to stefan lofvin at least until the next  general election  in september next year the pm may be  down but he's not yet  out paul brennan al jazeera
 

